    <briefdescription>
<para>the global time keeper, a singleton </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The global time keeper receives actual time stamps of all client threads and calculates the max time they are alloed to advance beyond systemc. All calculations are done based on ticks which is the minimal time step a simulator can do. The SystemC thread is special in that it is time wise always the last/slowest thread. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
